### Variable: makes it easy to change the base URL/port in one place
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001/api/notes

### 1. Get all notes
GET {{baseUrl}}

### 2. Get a single note by id (replace with a real id from the response of #1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/6a9e65096ae81762452fc76e

### 3. Create a new note (normal case, should return 200 + new object with id)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Ensure that everything still works",
  "important": true
}

### 4. Create a note without content field (should return 400 + { error: 'content missing' })
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "important": false
}

### 5. Delete a note (replace with a real id, should return 204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/6a9e64f86ae81762452fc76d

### 6. GET with a malformed id (should trigger CastError -> 400 { error: 'malformatted id' })
GET {{baseUrl}}/12345notavalidid

### 7. GET with a valid-format id that doesn't exist in the database (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/6741a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9ff

### 8. Hit a route that doesn't exist (should trigger unknownEndpoint -> 404 { error: 'unknown endpoint' })
GET http://localhost:3001/api/nonexistent

### 9. DELETE with a malformed id (CastError applies to DELETE too, not just GET -> 400 { error: 'malformatted id' })
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/12345notavalidid

### 10. DELETE with a valid-format id that doesn't exist (findByIdAndDelete does not error on a missing id,
### so this should still return 204, not 404 - a common gotcha worth testing explicitly)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/6741a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9ff

### 11. Create a note with content shorter than the schema's minlength
### Only returns 400 { error: '...' } (Mongoose ValidationError) if the schema has a minlength validator
### e.g. content: { type: String, minlength: 5, required: true }
### If the schema has no validators yet, this will currently succeed and just save "hi" as-is
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "hi",
  "important": false
}

### 12. Create a note with completely empty content string (tests required + minlength together)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "",
  "important": false
}

### 13. Send malformed JSON in the request body (missing closing brace)
### This fails inside express.json() itself, before it even reaches your route handler -
### tests what happens when the error isn't a CastError or ValidationError at all
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "broken json"
  "important": true